WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.884 --> 00:00:10.408
Once upon a time, there lived a little Dutch boy.

2
00:00:11.288 --> 00:00:15.092
No one knows if his story is true or what his name was.

3
00:00:15.993 --> 00:00:18.175
Most people today call him Hans.

4
00:00:19.135 --> 00:00:22.378
Hans lived in Haarlem, a city in the Netherlands.

5
00:00:23.179 --> 00:00:28.344
The city was built on very low ground near the sea and had many canals.

6
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:34.302
Bricklayers had built walls called dikes to control the water in the canals.

7
00:00:35.022 --> 00:00:37.163
The dikes kept the city from flooding.

8
00:00:38.824 --> 00:00:42.866
One autumn day Hans' mother made some delicious cakes.

9
00:00:44.006 --> 00:00:48.008
Hans thought of a blind man who lived on the other side of the city.

10
00:00:48.028 --> 00:00:51.629
"Mother, may I take some cakes to Mr.

11
00:00:51.689 --> 00:00:52.329
van Beek?"

12
00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:53.310
he asked.

13
00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:55.391
His mother smiled.

14
00:00:55.411 --> 00:00:58.212
"That's very kind of you."

15
00:00:59.176 --> 00:01:02.139
She helped Hans get ready, putting on his scarf.

16
00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:07.123
"Mr. van Beek loves to talk," his father said.

17
00:01:07.143 --> 00:01:08.924
"Don't stay too late.

18
00:01:09.524 --> 00:01:11.446
It looks like another storm is coming."

19
00:01:12.387 --> 00:01:14.268
The day was cold and windy.

20
00:01:15.209 --> 00:01:19.793
Hans skipped alongside the canals, full of water from the autumn rains.

21
00:01:20.653 --> 00:01:23.175
A while later he arrived at Mr.

22
00:01:23.236 --> 00:01:24.376
van Beek's house.

23
00:01:25.277 --> 00:01:28.500
Mr. van Beek was delighted to see his young friend.

24
00:01:32.832 --> 00:01:35.575
"I can't stay long today," Hans said.

25
00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:39.098
"But I'll come back soon to hear more stories!"

26
00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:45.063
Hans left and was still far from home when the weather became stormy.

27
00:01:45.684 --> 00:01:48.967
The wind burned his cheeks and whipped his scarf.

28
00:01:50.028 --> 00:01:54.832
Suddenly Hans spotted something—a small hole in a dike.

29
00:01:54.852 --> 00:01:57.374
"Uh-oh," he thought.

30
00:01:57.394 --> 00:01:59.216
"I need to find help."

31
00:02:00.532 --> 00:02:04.313
He knew that a small hole could become a bigger hole.

32
00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:08.634
If the hole became too big, the city might flood.

33
00:02:09.435 --> 00:02:12.195
Hans looked around, but he didn't see anyone.

34
00:02:12.215 --> 00:02:17.017
"Help!" he shouted, hoping someone would come running.

35
00:02:17.037 --> 00:02:22.138
He kept shouting until his throat felt dry, but no one came.

36
00:02:22.878 --> 00:02:25.319
He had to fix the problem on his own.

37
00:02:25.339 --> 00:02:27.840
"Oh, what can I do?"

38
00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:28.920
he thought.

39
00:02:29.764 --> 00:02:31.866
"I am only one little boy."

40
00:02:33.427 --> 00:02:35.369
Finally he got an idea.

41
00:02:36.009 --> 00:02:38.211
He wrapped his scarf around his hand.

42
00:02:39.072 --> 00:02:42.214
Then he pushed his fist into the hole.

43
00:02:42.855 --> 00:02:45.697
This stopped the water from coming through the dike.

44
00:02:46.478 --> 00:02:49.280
The stormy night went on and on.

45
00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.122
Hans shivered in the sharp wind.

46
00:02:52.142 --> 00:02:55.805
"I must be strong," thought Hans.

47
00:02:55.825 --> 00:02:59.328
"I must be brave like a grown-up."

48
00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:02.960
Hans grew weary.

49
00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:07.942
"I am so tired, but I must hold back the water."

50
00:03:09.042 --> 00:03:12.503
Morning finally came and the storm passed.

51
00:03:13.483 --> 00:03:15.524
An old man discovered Hans.

52
00:03:16.364 --> 00:03:18.365
His hand was still in the dike.

53
00:03:19.245 --> 00:03:22.246
He was shivering and exhausted from the cold.

54
00:03:23.406 --> 00:03:26.687
But he had held back the sea all night.

55
00:03:26.707 --> 00:03:29.608
"My goodness, child!"

56
00:03:30.048 --> 00:03:30.848
the man said.

57
00:03:31.648 --> 00:03:33.510
"What are you doing here?"

58
00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:39.495
"I'm holding back the water so the city won't flood," Hans said.

59
00:03:39.515 --> 00:03:41.997
"Don't move!

60
00:03:42.798 --> 00:03:44.299
I'll be right back!"

61
00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.142
The man hurried off to get help.

62
00:03:49.384 --> 00:03:52.146
Soon he was back with Hans' parents.

63
00:03:52.166 --> 00:03:54.608
"There you are, Hans!"

64
00:03:55.129 --> 00:03:56.209
his mother cried.

65
00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:58.752
"We searched for you all night long!"

66
00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:03.201
The city bricklayers came running to fix the dike.

67
00:04:04.181 --> 00:04:08.202
Hans pulled out his fist, and they quickly sealed the hole.

68
00:04:13.364 --> 00:04:15.184
did it," Hans thought.

69
00:04:16.665 --> 00:04:19.185
Hans was bundled up in warm clothes.

70
00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:24.287
He was very tired, but he smiled in the morning sun.

71
00:04:25.247 --> 00:04:28.528
The storm had passed and his city was safe.

72
00:04:29.844 --> 00:04:34.569
His mother and all the people of Haarlem were very proud of Hans.

73
00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:40.856
The next day, a bright morning, the mayor awarded Hans a medal.

74
00:04:42.017 --> 00:04:45.340
From that time on, Hans was known as the Little Hero of
